1
00:02:45,454 --> 00:02:51,454
He's facing the ultimate challenge. And fighting for his life.

2
00:05:30,909 --> 00:05:36,909
Rocky IV is a drama film directed by Sylvester Stallone.

3
00:08:16,363 --> 00:08:22,363
Rocky Balboa holds the world heavyweight championship, but a new challenger has stepped forward:
Drago, a six-foot-four, 261-pound fighter who has the backing of the Soviet Union.

4
00:11:01,818 --> 00:11:07,818
This time, Rocky's training regimen takes him to Siberia, where he
prepares for a globally televised match in the heart of Moscow.

5
00:13:47,272 --> 00:13:53,272
But nothing can truly prepare him for what he's about to face – a fight to the finish, in
which he must defend not only himself, but also the honor of his country!

6
00:16:32,727 --> 00:16:38,727
Robert "Rocky" Balboa, played by Sylvester Stallone.

7
00:19:18,181 --> 00:19:24,181
Ivan Drago, played by Dolph Lundgren.

8
00:22:03,636 --> 00:22:09,636
Apollo Creed, played by Carl Weathers.

9
00:24:49,090 --> 00:24:55,090
Adrianna "Adrian" Balboa, played by Talia Shire.

10
00:27:34,545 --> 00:27:40,545
Paulie Pennino, played by Burt Young.

11
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Ludmilla Vobet Drago, played by Brigitte Nielsen.

12
00:33:05,454 --> 00:33:11,454
Rocky IV is a 1985 American sports drama film starring,
written and directed by Sylvester Stallone.

13
00:35:50,909 --> 00:35:56,909
The film is the sequel to Rocky III (1982) and the
fourth installment in the Rocky franchise.

14
00:38:36,363 --> 00:38:42,363
It also stars Talia Shire, Burt Young, Carl Weathers,
Brigitte Nielsen, and Dolph Lundgren.

15
00:41:21,818 --> 00:41:27,818
In the film, Rocky Balboa (Stallone) confronts Ivan Drago (Lundgren), a Soviet
boxer responsible for another personal tragedy in Balboa's life.

16
00:44:07,272 --> 00:44:13,272
Development for a fourth Rocky film began soon after the success of Rocky III.

17
00:46:52,727 --> 00:46:58,727
Principal photography began in 1984, with filming locations
including Philadelphia, Wyoming, and Vancouver.

18
00:49:38,181 --> 00:49:44,181
Rocky IV was Lundgren's American film debut, and Stallone's last directorial effort until Rocky Balboa in 2006; they
engaged in authentic punching in their fight scenes, which led to Stallone being admitted to intensive care.

19
00:52:23,636 --> 00:52:29,636
Filming also featured new special effects and bona fide, groundbreaking sport
methods and equipment, some of which were years removed from public use.

20
00:55:09,090 --> 00:55:15,090
Rocky IV is known for its strong Cold War themes, as well as its successful theme
songs "Burning Heart" by Survivor and "Living in America" by James Brown.

21
00:57:54,545 --> 00:58:00,545
Rocky IV premiered in Los Angeles on November 21, 1985, and was theatrically
released in the United States by MGM/UA Entertainment Co.

22
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
under its United Artists label on November 27.

23
01:03:25,454 --> 01:03:31,454
The film initially received mixed reviews, with praise for Drago's
credibility as a villain, but criticized the predictable screenplay.

24
01:06:10,909 --> 01:06:16,909
Scholars note that Drago's ultimate defeat and the Soviet crowd's embrace of Rocky represented the dissolution of the Soviet
Union, while others criticized the film as propaganda through its Cold War themes and negative portrayals of Russians.

25
01:08:56,363 --> 01:09:02,363
Rocky IV grossed $300.5 million worldwide, becoming the highest-grossing Rocky film, the
third-highest-grossing US film of 1985 and the second-highest-grossing film worldwide.

26
01:11:41,818 --> 01:11:47,818
Later reviews were more favorable in the years later,
with praise for the training montages.

27
01:14:27,272 --> 01:14:33,272
The film is considered an icon of 1980s pop
culture, and gained a cult following.

28
01:17:12,727 --> 01:17:18,727
In 2021, a director's cut was released with the title Rocky IV: Rocky vs
Drago – The Ultimate Director's Cut, receiving positive reviews.

29
01:19:58,181 --> 01:20:04,181
A sequel, Rocky V, was released in 1990.

30
01:22:43,636 --> 01:22:49,636
The film's storylines are continued in Creed II (2018),
part of the sequel series to the Rocky films.

31
01:25:29,090 --> 01:25:35,090
The film explores themes of dying and death, friendship,
transporter, sports, loss of loved one.

32
01:28:14,545 --> 01:28:20,545
The tone is emotional.
